{"question_text": {"Surgery": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which investigation is essential before all major surgery? ", "option1": "Echocardiogram ", "option2": "Clotting profile ", "option3": "Full blood count ", "option4": "S. Albumin ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_383288056441751818872028.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_388592427431751818937699.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Which drug needs to be stopped  before an elective surgery in a patient with cardiac disease? ", "option1": "Beta-blocker ", "option2": "Rivaroxaban ", "option3": "Calcium channel blocker ", "option4": "Digoxin ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_619892209431751819020864.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Painful intermittent jaundice is seen in- ", "option1": "Choledocholithiasis ", "option2": "Periampullary carcinoma ", "option3": "Carcinoma head of pancreas ", "option4": "Cholelithiasis ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_459134606431751819103741.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Pigment gall stones are not associated with- ", "option1": "Liver cirrhosis ", "option2": "Biliary stent ", "option3": "Hereditary spherocytosis ", "option4": "Excess dietary iron ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_75306471451751819207451.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_528642891441751819189540.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_887435792431751819182414.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which is the most sensitive biochemical test for acute pancreatitis? ", "option1": "S. amylase ", "option2": "S. lipase ", "option3": "Fecal elastase ", "option4": "Urinary amylase ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_596110152431751819278306.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which is not characteristic of hypovolemic shock? ", "option1": "Low cardiac output ", "option2": "Low mixed venous saturation ", "option3": "Low venous pressure ", "option4": "Low vascular resistance ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_298544806431751808795435.png\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) In hemorrhagic shock, how much loss of circulating volume causes hypotension?  ", "option1": "10% ", "option2": "15% ", "option3": "20% ", "option4": "30% ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<!--StartFragment--><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;\">In general, </span><span style=\"font-size: 18.0pt; font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: +mn-ea; mso-bidi-font-family: +mn-cs; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #00b050; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; language: en-US; font-weight: bold; mso-style-textfill-type: solid; mso-style-textfill-fill-color: #00B050; mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha: 100.0%;\">loss of around 15% of the circulating blood volume is within normal compensatory mechanisms</span><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;\">. </span><span style=\"font-size: 18.0pt; font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: +mn-ea; mso-bidi-font-family: +mn-cs; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #c55a11; mso-color-index: 5; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; language: en-US; font-weight: bold; mso-style-textfill-type: solid; mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor: accent2; mso-style-textfill-fill-color: #C55A11; mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha: 100.0%; mso-style-textfill-fill-colortransforms: lumm=75000;\">Blood pressure is usually well maintained and only falls after 30&ndash;40% of circulating volume has been lost.&nbsp;</span><!--EndFragment-->"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Which is the surest sign of compartment syndrome? ", "option1": "Paraesthesia ", "option2": "Pain on passive stretching ", "option3": "Paralysis ", "option4": "Pulselessness ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_999350641511751809752626.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_682222079501751809745400.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Secondary hemorrhage is caused by- ", "option1": "Dislodgement of clot ", "option2": "Slipped ligature ", "option3": "Sloughing of vessel wall ", "option4": "Vasodilatation ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<!--StartFragment-->\r\n<p style=\"language: en-GB; line-height: 150%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: 0in; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; mso-line-break-override: none; word-break: normal; punctuation-wrap: hanging;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;\">Secondary hemorrhage usually </span><span style=\"font-size: 18.0pt; font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: +mn-ea; mso-bidi-font-family: +mn-cs; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #00b050; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; language: en-US; font-weight: bold; mso-style-textfill-type: solid; mso-style-textfill-fill-color: #00B050; mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha: 100.0%;\">occurs 7-14 days after injury</span><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;\">. </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"language: en-GB; line-height: 150%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: 0in; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; mso-line-break-override: none; word-break: normal; punctuation-wrap: hanging;\"><u><span style=\"font-size: 18.0pt; font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: +mn-ea; mso-bidi-font-family: +mn-cs; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #c55a11; mso-color-index: 5; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; language: en-US; font-weight: bold; mso-style-textfill-type: solid; mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor: accent2; mso-style-textfill-fill-color: #C55A11; mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha: 100.0%; mso-style-textfill-fill-colortransforms: lumm=75000;\">Cause:</span></u><span style=\"font-size: 18.0pt; font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: +mn-ea; mso-bidi-font-family: +mn-cs; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #00b050; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; language: en-US; font-weight: bold; mso-style-textfill-type: solid; mso-style-textfill-fill-color: #00B050; mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha: 100.0%;\">Sloughing of the wall of a vessel</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"language: en-GB; line-height: 150%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: 0in; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; mso-line-break-override: none; word-break: normal; punctuation-wrap: hanging;\"><u><span style=\"font-size: 18.0pt; font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: +mn-ea; mso-bidi-font-family: +mn-cs; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; color: #c55a11; mso-color-index: 5; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; language: en-US; font-weight: bold; mso-style-textfill-type: solid; mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor: accent2; mso-style-textfill-fill-color: #C55A11; mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha: 100.0%; mso-style-textfill-fill-colortransforms: lumm=75000;\">Precipitating factors: </span></u></p>\r\n<div style=\"language: en-GB; line-height: 150%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: .75in; text-indent: -.38in; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; mso-line-break-override: none; word-break: normal; punctuation-wrap: hanging;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-special-format: bullet; font-family: Arial;\">- </span></span><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;\">Infection</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"language: en-GB; line-height: 150%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: .75in; text-indent: -.38in; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; mso-line-break-override: none; word-break: normal; punctuation-wrap: hanging;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-special-format: bullet; font-family: Arial;\">- </span></span><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;\">Pressure necrosis from drain<br /></span><span style=\"font-family: Calibri; font-size: 18pt;\">- Malignancy&nbsp;</span></div>\r\n<!--EndFragment-->"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which is an example of dirty wound? ", "option1": "Open fracture ", "option2": "Acute appendicitis ", "option3": "Cholecystectomy ", "option4": "Fecal peritonitis ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_260623096431751810220768.png\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Pseudomembranous colitis is caused by- ", "option1": "Clostridium welchii", "option2": "Clostridium botulinum ", "option3": "Clostridium difficile ", "option4": "Clostridium septicum ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_624936400431751810554695.png\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Which is the most common symptom of tetanus? ", "option1": "Trismus ", "option2": "Risus sardonicus ", "option3": "Dysphagia", "option4": "Hyperacusis ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_979704542441751810684152.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_722239867431751810676725.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Which hernia is caused by inadequate muscular strength? ", "option1": "Direct inguinal hernia ", "option2": "Diaphragmatic hernia", "option3": "Femoral hernia ", "option4": "Indirect inguinal hernia ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_924259982441751811814555.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_875496975431751811806206.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Direct inguinal hernia can be differentiated from indirect hernia clinically by- ", "option1": "Cough impulse ", "option2": "Transillumination test ", "option3": "Reducibility", "option4": "Deep ring occlusion test", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_120298713431751812192044.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Superficial burn is characterized by- ", "option1": "Hard leathery feel ", "option2": "Diminished sensation ", "option3": "Blistering ", "option4": "No capillary return ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_136166693431751812498480.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Which is the key parameter to monitor while resuscitating a burn patient? ", "option1": "Blood pressure ", "option2": "Pulse rate ", "option3": "Cardiac output ", "option4": "Urine output ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_823739533431751812800835.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Which IV fluid contains lactate? ", "option1": "Hartmann solution ", "option2": "Cholera saline ", "option3": "Normal saline ", "option4": "5% dextrose in aqua ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_904622957431751812929615.png\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Which is the strongest risk factor basal cell carcinoma? ", "option1": "Arsenicosis ", "option2": "Sunlight exposure ", "option3": "Coal tar", "option4": "Choronic scars ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_663715241431751813224770.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Which is the most common site of carcinoid tumour? ", "option1": "Stomach ", "option2": "Vermiform appendix ", "option3": "Rectum ", "option4": "Terminal ileum ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_86525987431751813413952.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Which is the confirmatory test for gastroesophageal reflux disease? ", "option1": "High resolution manometry", "option2": "Upper GI endoscopy ", "option3": "Ambulatory pH recording ", "option4": "Barium swallow X-ray ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_415527880441751813602159.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_744803569431751813593870.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Which is a radiological feature of small bowel obstruction? ", "option1": "Haustral folds ", "option2": "Tyre like shadows ", "option3": "Multiple air-fluid level", "option4": "Peripheral distension ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_845079614431751814102017.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Which is not a clinical sign of acute appendicitis? ", "option1": "Psoas sign ", "option2": "Rovsing sign ", "option3": "Cullen's sign ", "option4": "Pointing sign ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_779988063441751814216201.png\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_391877991431751814199567.png\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Which is not an indication for urethral catheterization? ", "option1": "Chronic retention ", "option2": "Urodynamic study", "option3": "Acute retention ", "option4": "Urethral injury", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_346535622431751814348381.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Contraindication of circumcision is- ", "option1": "Phimosis ", "option2": "Hypospadias ", "option3": "Lichen sclerosis ", "option4": "Recurrent UTI ", "answer": "2", "exp": "Circumcision is contraindicated in hypospadias because the foreskin is used to reconstruct the urethra during hypospadias surgery.&nbsp;<br /><br />All other options here are indications for circumcision.<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_163740015431751819798342.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Which one of these surgical procedures has the highest risk of developing DVT? ", "option1": "Cardiothoracic surgery ", "option2": "Inguinal hernia repair ", "option3": "Appendicectomy ", "option4": "Total knee replacement ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_74116702431751814793401.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Loss of consciousness with a lucid interval is characteristic of- ", "option1": "Extradural hematoma ", "option2": "Subdoral hematoma ", "option3": "Subarachnoid hemorrhage ", "option4": "Intracerebral hematoma ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_440614046431751815023686.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Which is the most common type of renal cell carcinoma? ", "option1": "Papillary RCC", "option2": "Clear-cell RCC", "option3": "Chromophobe RCC", "option4": "Medullary carcinoma ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_10970614431751815188296.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Which is the commonest cause of epistaxis in children? ", "option1": "Foreign bodies ", "option2": "Enlarged adenoids ", "option3": "Nose picking ", "option4": "Haemophilia", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_417398539441751821928998.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_548027186431751821920531.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Which thyroid swelling cannot be diagnosed by FNAC? ", "option1": "Follicular carcinoma ", "option2": "Medullary carcinoma ", "option3": "Papillary carcinoma ", "option4": "Lymphoma ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_682303897431751815653158.png\" />"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Which is the tumour marker for medullary carcinoma of thyroid? ", "option1": "Calcitonin ", "option2": "Thyroglobulin ", "option3": "TSH-RAb", "option4": "Thyroxine ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_623651391501751815833255.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) Which is not routinely done for triple assesment of breast swelling? ", "option1": "Ultrasound ", "option2": "Core biopsy ", "option3": "Clinical examination ", "option4": "MRI ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_130472808501751815983962.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Which is the most common cause of breast lump in young women? ", "option1": "Fibroadenoma ", "option2": "Duct ectasia ", "option3": "Mondor's disease ", "option4": "Carcinoma ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_833196506431751816099325.png\" />"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Which is not a treatment option for hydrocele? ", "option1": "Eversion of sac ", "option2": "Plication ", "option3": "Aspiration", "option4": "Mesh repair ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_271924310431751816818855.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) Which is the most common cause of chronic pancreatitis? ", "option1": "Gall stone ", "option2": "Alcoholism ", "option3": "Trauma ", "option4": "Pancreatic cancer ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_977201632431751816929473.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) Which is the most common symptom of esophageal cancer? ", "option1": "Progressive dysphagia ", "option2": "Heartburn ", "option3": "Hoarseness of voice ", "option4": "Hematemesis", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_482963709431751817129645.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) Which is the first step in managing a polytrauma patient? ", "option1": "Protect cervical spine", "option2": "Correct hypovolemia", "option3": "Exposure ", "option4": "Evaluate neurological status ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_461366259491751817392618.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) Which nerve is commonly injured in shoulder dislocation? ", "option1": "Radial nerve ", "option2": "Ulnar nerve ", "option3": "Axillary nerve ", "option4": "Median nerve ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_551361965431751817576506.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) Which is the most common site of acute osteomyelitis in children? ", "option1": "Vertebra ", "option2": "Pelvis ", "option3": "Elbow ", "option4": "Upper tibia ", "answer": "4", "exp": "In children, long bones are commonly affected. Upper end of tibia, lower end of femur and upper end of femur are the commonest sites.&nbsp;<br /><br />In adults, vertebra is commonly affected.&nbsp;<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_304587002491751818010675.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) Which is the metabolic abnormality in gastric outlet obstruction? ", "option1": "Hypochloremic hyperkalemic alkalosis ", "option2": "Hypochloremic hypokalemic acidosis ", "option3": "Hyperchloremic hypokalemic alkalosis ", "option4": "Hypochloremic hypokalemic alkalosis ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_601233956431751818218466.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "40", "question": "৪০) Muddy colored nipple discharge is caused by- ", "option1": "Paget's disease ", "option2": "Duct ectasia ", "option3": "Ductal carcinoma", "option4": "Duct papilloma ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_691757849431751818796812.png\" />"}], "Pathology": [{"id": "41", "question": "৪১) Which is the permanent cells of human body -", "option1": "Fibroblast", "option2": "Epithelial tissue", "option3": "Neuron", "option4": "Smooth muscle cell", "answer": "3", "exp": "Explanation:<br />Permanent cells are cells that have lost the ability to divide (i.e., they are non-proliferative after birth).<br />Once destroyed, they cannot be replaced through mitosis.<br />These cells remain in the G₀ phase of the cell cycle permanently.<br /><br />&nbsp;Examples of Permanent Cells in the Human Body:<br />1. Neurons (Nerve cells) &ndash; Central nervous system neurons do not divide.<br />2. Cardiac muscle cells &ndash; Myocytes in the heart do not regenerate.<br />3. Skeletal muscle cells &ndash; Multinucleated skeletal muscle fibers are also considered permanent, although satellite cells can aid limited repair."}, {"id": "42", "question": "৪২) Following which is oncogenic RNA virus -", "option1": "Human T cell lymphotrophic virus", "option2": "Hepatitis B virus", "option3": "Epstein Barr virus", "option4": "HPV virus", "answer": "1", "exp": "Explanation :<br />Oncogenic RNA Viruses:<br /><br />1. Human T-cell leukemia virus type 1 (HTLV-1)<br />&ndash; Causes adult T-cell leukemia/lymphoma.<br /><br /><br />2. Hepatitis C virus (HCV)<br />&ndash; Associated with hepatocellular carcinoma (liver cancer)."}, {"id": "43", "question": "৪৩) What is the example of distributive shock -", "option1": "Myocardial infraction", "option2": "Intestinal fistula", "option3": "Anaphylaxis", "option4": "Thyrotoxic crisis", "answer": "3", "exp": "Explanation :<br />Examples of distribtive shock :<br />Septic shock<br />Anaphylaxis&nbsp;<br />Spinal cord injury"}, {"id": "44", "question": "৪৪) What is the most reliable diagnostic test for detecting H. pylori infection?", "option1": "Stool antigen test", "option2": "Serology", "option3": "Urea breath test", "option4": "Endoscopy", "answer": "3", "exp": "Explanation:<br />The urea breath test is highly sensitive and specific for detecting active H. pylori infection."}, {"id": "45", "question": "৪৫) Following which is example of autosomal recessive trait -", "option1": "Hemophilia A& B", "option2": "Alport syndrome", "option3": "Neurofibromatosis", "option4": "Galactosemia", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG-20250706-WA0008.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"597\" height=\"560\" />"}, {"id": "46", "question": "৪৬) Which of the following is a hallmark of megaloblastic anemia on PBF?", "option1": "Hypersegmented neutrophils", "option2": "Howell-Jolly bodies", "option3": "Heinz bodies", "option4": "Basophilic stippling", "answer": "1", "exp": "Explanation:<br />Hypersegmented neutrophils (&ge;5 lobes) are classic in vitamin B12 or folate deficiency."}, {"id": "47", "question": "৪৭) Cytokine of acute inflammation -", "option1": "IL-1", "option2": "IL-12", "option3": "Gumma interferon", "option4": "IL-17", "answer": "1", "exp": "Explanation :<br />Cytokine of acute inflammation :<br />TNF, IL-1, IL-6, Chemokines<br />Cytokine of chronic inflammation :<br />IL-12, Gumma interferon, IL-17, All mediators of acute inflammation&nbsp;"}, {"id": "48", "question": "৪৮) Which of the following is a complication of gonorrhea in neonates?", "option1": "Neonatal jaundice", "option2": "Ophthalmia neonatorum", "option3": "Neonatal sepsis", "option4": "Aseptic meningitis", "answer": "2", "exp": "Explanation:<br />Gonorrhea can be transmitted during birth, causing severe conjunctivitis (ophthalmia neonatorum)."}, {"id": "49", "question": "৪৯)  Which medication reduces disease flares of SLE -", "option1": "Hydroxychloroquine", "option2": "Methotrexate", "option3": "Prednisolone", "option4": "Azathioprine", "answer": "1", "exp": "Explanation:<br />Hydroxychloroquine is the mainstay of long-term therapy, reduces flares, and long term survival against SLE."}, {"id": "50", "question": "৫০)  What is the most common cause of hyperthyroidism?", "option1": "Toxic multinodular goiter", "option2": "Thyroid adenoma", "option3": "Graves’ disease", "option4": "Subacute thyroiditis", "answer": "3", "exp": "Explanation:<br />Graves&rsquo; disease is the most common cause, especially in younger females.<br />It is an autoimmune condition with TSH receptor-stimulating antibodies."}], "Forensic Medicine": [{"id": "51", "question": "৫১) A doctor who observed an accident and is called to court to narrate what he saw is known as:", "option1": "Expert witness", "option2": "Common witness", "option3": "Hostile witness", "option4": "Anonymous witness", "answer": "2", "exp": "A common witness gives facts based on what they have seen, heard, or perceived."}, {"id": "52", "question": "৫২) Evidence of recent intercourse can be best found by:", "option1": "Hymenal tear", "option2": "Presence of semen in vaginal smear", "option3": "Bruises on thighs", "option4": "Pubic hair collection", "answer": "2", "exp": "Microscopic detection of spermatozoa is crucial in establishing intercourse."}, {"id": "53", "question": "৫৩) According to BPC Section 320, which of the following is not grievous hurt?", "option1": "Emasculation", "option2": "Tooth loss", "option3": "Simple abrasion", "option4": "Loss of vision in one eye", "answer": "3", "exp": "Abrasion is a simple injury; others fall under grievous hurt."}, {"id": "54", "question": "৫৪) A DNA test result submitted by the forensic lab is categorized under:", "option1": "Circumstantial evidence", "option2": "Oral evidence", "option3": "Primary evidence", "option4": "Documentary evidence", "answer": "4", "exp": "Written reports and scientific findings are considered documentary evidence under the Evidence Act."}, {"id": "55", "question": "৫৫) A medico-legal report on a rape victim must contain:", "option1": "Doctor’s opinion on guilt", "option2": "Mention of “habituated to sex”", "option3": "Factual findings without interpretation", "option4": "Statement on whether rape occurred", "answer": "3", "exp": "Doctors should report injuries and findings but not conclude whether rape occurred &mdash; that is a legal decision."}, {"id": "56", "question": "৫৬) Barr body identification is useful in:", "option1": "Estimating age", "option2": "Sex determination", "option3": "Time since death", "option4": "Identity of twins", "answer": "2", "exp": "Presence of Barr body (inactive X chromosome) confirms female chromosomal sex (XX)."}, {"id": "57", "question": "৫৭) A patient refuses a life-saving blood transfusion due to religious beliefs. The doctor should:", "option1": "Proceed anyway to save life", "option2": "Obtain court permission", "option3": "Respect the patient’s refusal after informed consent", "option4": "Call the police", "answer": "3", "exp": "Respecting informed refusal is a key aspect of autonomy in medical ethics, even in life-threatening cases."}, {"id": "58", "question": "৫৮) A medical practitioner must record a dying declaration in the presence of –", "option1": "Police officer", "option2": "Relative", "option3": "Magistrate", "option4": "Attending nurse", "answer": "3", "exp": "A dying declaration should ideally be recorded by a magistrate. However, in the absence of one, a doctor can record it, ensuring voluntariness and mental fitness."}, {"id": "59", "question": "৫৯) The term “res ipsa loquitur” in medical negligence implies –", "option1": "The patient is always right", "option2": "The physician must prove innocence", "option3": "The thing speaks for itself", "option4": "A civil suit is mandatory", "answer": "3", "exp": "This doctrine implies that the nature of the injury is so evident that negligence is presumed unless proven otherwise."}, {"id": "60", "question": "৬০) The most accurate method of sex determination from bones is –", "option1": "Pelvis examination", "option2": "Skull measurement", "option3": "Long bone length", "option4": "Mandible angle", "answer": "1", "exp": "Pelvic bones show the most distinct differences between sexes and are considered the most accurate."}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 11535, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "1800000", "is_omr": true, "omr_time": "2160000", "examname": "Jul 07, 2025", "type": "BCS-Health-Mock", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}